From f45d75ce71e5d21737464060e279caba870cff54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:48:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scratch: PP_HOMEVEC / PP_HOMEDIR home senses, plus the
 come-home and trail teachers ported onto the compute branch

PP_HOMEVEC=R:W (off by default): a home vector that stays sharp far out. far = clamp((d-R)/W, 0, 1) on context
slot 9 (d_alarm, 0 on every bed decision) and, per option, f::LAST_FOOD (unwritten until now) = cos-to-home * far.
Both exactly 0 within R of home. PP_HOMEDIR=1: f::BUILDING = cos-to-home at every distance (for trail rule 2).
A genome's live links on those slots must be zeroed first (hA1: 16 on slot 9, 8 on f40, 11 on f18).

Ported (3-way) from the starve-trace thread's homefar-farctx-vs-9d19121c-with-shadow-rim.patch (PP_CARRY,
PP_HOMEFAR, PP_FAR_CTX, the carry/sampler copy-log fields, PP_SHADOW) and the maze thread's
trail-teacher-vs-ee38ae5b.patch (PP_TRAIL_LABEL / PP_TRAIL_OUT / PP_TRAIL_ACT; its label shares copy-log field 16
when the carry teacher has none). Parts of the shadow-rim patch already on this branch (pack move, PP_NEEDDROP,
PP_NOMIND) keep this branch's version.

Off: inrun seed 1 (hA1) byte-identical to 529ff42a in every output but events.csv, which gains the shadow-rim
patch's `fdrop` rows (identical with them filtered out). Bed (come-home settings, sel=off, 32 seeds) reproduces the
starve-trace thread's hA1 row exactly (4.31 starved per 24, 2.69 past 60 cols, home 269, cuts 320) and the maze
thread's sup / supOut rows.

Measured, 32 seeds, starved per 24 (past 60 cols): hA1 4.31 (2.69); hA1 with slot 9 + f40 zeroed and PP_HOMEVEC=40:30
3.66 (2.62); teacher acting (PP_CARRY=1 PP_HOMEFAR=45) 2.28 (0.75); copy hc1 (only the sense's 48 weights trained)
2.50 (0.75), home food 268, new cuts 315.

